    "summary": "Malietoa Tanumafili II (4 January 1913 – 11 May 2007) was O le Ao o le Malo (head of state) of Samoa from its independence in 1962 until his death in 2007. He was bestowed with the Malietoa title in 1940 and had previously worked for the New Zealand administration as a civil servant and parliamentarian.",
